## Structure

```
src/
├── main.ts                  ← starts the server (and ORM connection, if any)
├── app.ts                   ← builds the Koa app; separate from main.ts so tests can import it directly
├── config/env.ts            ← the only file that reads process.env
├── middlewares/              ← error handling, validation glue
├── shared/                   ← database/cache clients used by more than one module
└── routes/<module>/
    ├── <module>.entity.ts      ← the model{{#if ormTypeorm}} (also the TypeORM persistence entity){{/if}}
    ├── <module>.repository.ts  ← data access
    ├── <module>.service.ts     ← business logic
    ├── <module>.controller.ts  ← Koa ctx handlers
    ├── <module>.routes.ts      ← wires repository → service → controller → router (manual, no DI container)
{{#if hasValidation}}
    └── <module>.validation.ts  ← request validation
{{/if}}
```

Call direction: `routes` wires everything → `controller` → `service` → `repository`. A layer only ever talks to the one directly below it.

